  "plain": "An author, Whitley Strieber, told podcast host Jesse Michels about a paper said to come from the 1950s. Strieber says a general named Arthur Exon, who was not a scientist but had spent time around scientists working on UFOs, spoke of a paper by the scientist John von Neumann. As Strieber tells it, the paper said the strange presence behind UFOs has to be believed in before it can fully enter our reality, which would mean human belief plays a part in the phenomenon."
